\pard\widctlpar\sa160\sl276\slmult1\kerning2\b\f0\fs52\lang16393 Transformer Architecture in Detail\par
\fs24 1. Introduction\par
\b0 Transformer Architecture is a deep learning model introduced in 2017 through the research paper \b "Attention Is All You Need."\b0  It revolutionized Natural Language Processing (NLP) and became the foundation of modern AI systems such as GPT, BERT, Gemini, Claude, Llama, and Microsoft Copilot. Unlike traditional neural networks such as Recurrent Neural Networks (RNNs) and Long Short-Term Memory (LSTMs), Transformers process all input tokens simultaneously, enabling faster training and better understanding of context.\par
\b Key Highlights\par

\pard{\pntext\f4\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf4\pnindent360{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\sa160\sl276\slmult1\b0 Introduced in 2017 by Google researchers.\par
{\pntext\f4\'B7\tab}Foundation of Large Language Models (LLMs).\par
{\pntext\f4\'B7\tab}Uses Self-Attention instead of recurrence.\par
{\pntext\f4\'B7\tab}Supports parallel processing.\par
{\pntext\f4\'B7\tab}Handles long-range dependencies effectively.\par

\pard\widctlpar\sa160\sl276\slmult1\par
\b 2. Why Transformers Were Introduced\par
\b0 Before Transformers, NLP tasks relied heavily on RNNs and LSTMs. These models processed text sequentially, causing challenges in handling long sentences and increasing training time.\par
\b Limitations of RNNs and LSTMs\par

\pard{\pntext\f4\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf4\pnindent360{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\sa160\sl276\slmult1\b0 Sequential processing leads to slower training.\par
{\pntext\f4\'B7\tab}Difficulty remembering information from distant words.\par
{\pntext\f4\'B7\tab}Vanishing and exploding gradient problems.\par
{\pntext\f4\'B7\tab}Poor scalability for large datasets.\par

\pard\widctlpar\sa160\sl276\slmult1\b How Transformers Solve These Problems\par

\pard{\pntext\f4\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf4\pnindent360{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\sa160\sl276\slmult1\b0 Process words in parallel.\par
{\pntext\f4\'B7\tab}Use attention mechanisms to capture context.\par
{\pntext\f4\'B7\tab}Improve training efficiency.\par
{\pntext\f4\'B7\tab}Scale effectively for billions of parameters.\par

\pard\widctlpar\sa160\sl276\slmult1\par
\b 3. Overall Architecture\par
\b0 A Transformer consists of two primary components:\par
\b Encoder\par
\b0 The Encoder processes the input sequence and learns its contextual representation.\par
\b Decoder\par
\b0 The Decoder uses the encoded information to generate outputs sequentially.\par
\b Architecture Flow\par
