\b 10. Residual Connections\par
\b0 Deep neural networks often lose information when data passes through many layers.\par
Residual Connections solve this issue.\par
\b Formula\par
\b0 Output = Input + Layer Output\par
\b Benefits\par

\pard{\pntext\f4\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf4\pnindent360{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\sa160\sl276\slmult1\b0 Prevents information loss.\par
{\pntext\f4\'B7\tab}Improves gradient flow.\par
{\pntext\f4\'B7\tab}Enables deeper networks.\par

\pard\widctlpar\sa160\sl276\slmult1\par
\b 11. Layer Normalization\par
\b0 Layer Normalization stabilizes learning by maintaining consistent activation values.\par
\b Benefits\par

\pard{\pntext\f4\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf4\pnindent360{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\sa160\sl276\slmult1\b0 Faster convergence.\par
{\pntext\f4\'B7\tab}Stable training.\par
{\pntext\f4\'B7\tab}Better performance.\par

