\pard\widctlpar\sa160\sl276\slmult1\par
\b 19. Conclusion\par
\b0 Transformer Architecture is the technological foundation behind modern Artificial Intelligence and Generative AI systems. Its innovative use of Self-Attention, Multi-Head Attention, Positional Encoding, Feed Forward Networks, Residual Connections, and Layer Normalization enables models to understand context more effectively than previous architectures. By overcoming the limitations of RNNs and LSTMs, Transformers have made possible advanced AI systems such as GPT, BERT, Gemini, Claude, and Microsoft Copilot. Today, Transformers power applications ranging from conversational AI and content generation to healthcare, finance, software development, and enterprise automation, making them one of the most important breakthroughs in the history of Artificial Intelligence.\par
